#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# weierstrass_p_prime

#% text
# `weierstrass_p_prime(u, [g2, g3])` gives the derivative of the Weierstrass elliptic function `p(u; g2, g3)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `p'` is odd, with a triple pole `-2/u^3` at the lattice points; `p'^2 = 4 p^3 - g2 p - g3`.

#% item
# Numerical values as for `weierstrass_p`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
weierstrass_p_prime(0.5, [1, 2])
#% output
#= -15.914060722103613

#% cell
n(weierstrass_p_prime(1/3, [1, 2]), 30)
#% output
#= -53.9560603135463961472930874211945

#% cell
weierstrass_p_prime(3.3 + 2*im, [12, -7])
#% output
#= -2.958694511659682 + 2.942073982341144im

#% text
# A difference quotient of `weierstrass_p`:

#% cell
(weierstrass_p(0.8 + 1.0e-6, [1, 2]) - weierstrass_p(0.8 - 1.0e-6, [1, 2]))/2.0e-6 - weierstrass_p_prime(0.8, [1, 2])
#% output
#= -1.1512968356441888e-10

